WEBVTT

00:00:00.161 --> 00:00:04.600
GPU rental products differ in how much infrastructure the customer manages.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.645
Major cloud providers integrate GPU instances with mature identity, networking, storage,

00:00:09.645 --> 00:00:11.415
monitoring, and compliance services.

00:00:11.415 --> 00:00:16.390
Specialized GPU clouds may offer a wider accelerator selection or simpler pricing.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.460
Marketplace platforms can provide economical capacity from multiple hosts,

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.770
but hardware consistency, trust boundaries, support, networking,

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.871
and data-erasure assurances require careful review.

00:00:25.871 --> 00:00:28.890
Hosted notebooks are convenient for experiments and learning because an interactive

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.400
environment can start quickly.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.580
They may have session limits, temporary storage, restricted networking,

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.625
or less control over system packages.

00:00:35.625 --> 00:00:39.395
Dedicated instances provide an operating system and administrative control,

00:00:39.395 --> 00:00:42.730
making them suitable for custom environments and persistent services,

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.607
but the renter owns patching, firewall rules, credentials, and shutdown.

00:00:46.607 --> 00:00:50.095
Serverless-style inference services hide much of the machine lifecycle and bill by

00:00:50.095 --> 00:00:50.800
request,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.255
execution time, or reserved endpoint capacity.

00:00:53.255 --> 00:00:57.500
They can reduce operations for supported models, though cold starts, model restrictions,

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.115
data handling, and pricing at sustained volume must be evaluated.

00:01:01.115 --> 00:01:05.810
A managed endpoint and a raw GPU instance solve different problems even when both run the

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:06.480
same model.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.586
On-demand pricing favors flexibility.

00:01:08.586 --> 00:01:12.560
Reserved or committed capacity can lower cost for predictable long-term use.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.260
Spot or interruptible capacity offers discounts because the provider may reclaim it,

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.315
making it appropriate for restartable and checkpointed work.

00:01:19.315 --> 00:01:23.418
Also verify regions, quotas, minimum billing, support, and actual inventory.

00:01:23.418 --> 00:01:26.720
Select the service model that matches the job's duration, control needs,

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.070
interruption tolerance, and data sensitivity,

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.350
not simply the lowest advertised hourly rate.
